JsEdit - the programmer's editor
================================

!JsEdit, in the Apps directory, is a text editor for programs, in the
style of the programmers' editors of the time (StrongED, Zap). It is
built on Edit, so Edit's menus, Find and keys all work in it too.

  - It colours JavaScript, BBC BASIC, Obey and JSON as you type,
    numbers the lines and keeps your indentation.
  - It completes names from the desktop's programming interface as you
    type (Ctrl-Space to ask).
  - It checks a JavaScript program's syntax as you type and marks the
    first mistake.
  - Run (Ctrl-R) saves the program and runs it. If it goes wrong, the
    error comes back to the line it happened on (throwback), and the
    Throwback window lists it.
  - The Functions button lists the functions in a program: click one
    to go to it.
  - Display > Dark theme, and programming fonts, on the menu.


Starting
--------

Double-click !JsEdit. Its icon appears on the icon bar.

  SELECT on the icon         a new JavaScript program
  MENU on the icon           Info, Create (a new file of another
                             kind), Open directory, Throwback, Quit
  Drag a file to the icon    edit it
  Drag a directory there     see all its files in a directory view

To edit a JavaScript program (a JSScript file) from a directory
display, Shift-double-click it: a plain double-click runs it.


Directory views
---------------

A directory view shows a directory's files as a tree, with the Filer's
icons. Drag a directory, or an application, onto the JsEdit icon, or
use Open directory on its menu.

  - Click the arrow by a directory to open or shut it.
  - Double-click a file to edit it. Files that aren't text run, as they
    would from the Filer; hold Shift to edit them as text anyway.
  - Files you're editing are shown in bold, with * after the name when
    they have changes that aren't saved.
  - MENU gives New file, New directory, Rename, Delete, Select all,
    Expand all, Collapse all, Find in files (every line containing some
    text, in all the files: click one to go to it), Open in Filer and
    Refresh.
  - Drag files to a Filer window to copy them there, or from the Filer
    into the view to copy them in (hold Shift to move them).
  - The keys: arrows, Return to open, Delete, and letters to go to a
    name.

The views open when you quit JsEdit come back next time.


More
----

!JsEdit's !Help file (MENU over it in a directory display, Help)
describes the toolbar, the keys and the mode files that set the
colours. The book "Programming in JavaScript" (see the guide
Programming) uses JsEdit from its first chapter.
